 "about": "Ruler lists written for GeoHistory from general knowledge, for major states whose rulers Wikidata does not file under the state shown on the map. Each row is [name, first year, last year, English Wikipedia title (when it differs from the name)]; BC years are negative. tools/build_rulers.py checks every row against the Wikidata item of the linked article (dates of the offices the person held, and years of death) and writes the result to tools/cache/curated_rulers.json; a row counts as verified only when both its years are confirmed. 'approx' lists carry conventional dates that scholars give with a few years of variation: they are checked with 5 years of slack and shown with 'c.'.",
